// BACKEND: interpreter
// OUTPUT: 3
// OUTPUT: 4
// OUTPUT: 2
//
// Regression test for the builtin-signature unification.
//
// Before the unification, the analyzer and verifier used
// `List<Unknown>` for `List.length`'s parameter, but the IR builder
// used `List<Float>`. The builder's tighter signature rejected
// `List.length(names)` where `names: List<String>`, even though the
// call is well-typed. The unification made all three sites read
// `List<Unknown>` from `crate::builtins`, so this program compiles
// and runs.
//
// If the `List<Float>` signature is ever reintroduced at any site,
// this test fails at compile time before it can fail at runtime.
proc main
    val names := ["alice", "bob", "carol"]
    print(List.length(names))

    val ints := [10, 20, 30, 40]
    print(List.length(ints))

    val floats := [1.0, 2.0]
    print(List.length(floats))
